            <ArticleTitle>Microsatellite Expansion Diseases: Repeat Toxicity Found in Translation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>249-251</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0896-6273(17)30001-6</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.neuron.2017.01.001</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Sellier et al. (2017) show that translation of expanded CGG repeats in fragile X-associated tremor/ataxia syndrome is initiated at an upstream ACG near-cognate start codon. The resulting polyglycine-containing protein, but not repeat RNA, is pathogenic by disrupting the nuclear lamina.</AbstractText>
